    "problem": "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{'}(t) &=-2x(t)-5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{'}(t) &=5x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1,2}=-2\\pm 5\\text{i},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1,2}=[\\pm \\text{i},1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}(5t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}(5t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in \\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nFor example, when ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we obtain the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &={{field-1}} \\\\ y &={{field-2}}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\"> <tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\"> <td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$t$</td> <td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td> <td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\frac{\\pi }{20}$</td> <td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\frac{\\pi }{10}$</td> </tr> <tr data-next-row=\"true\"> <td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</td> <td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td> <td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.52$</td> <td data-cell-align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td> </tr> <tr> <td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td> <td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td> <td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.52$</td> <td data-cell-align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td> </tr> </tbody></table></div>\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](https://mathacademy.com/graphics/3a7363e073214596